        "heading_ibUpnR": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "An Heirloom in the Making",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_k3fqfX": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "enlarge_text": true,
            "text": "<p>Le Creuset introduced the first colorful enameled cast iron cookware in 1925, in its signature orange Flame. A century later, every piece of Le Creuset enameled cast iron is still made at the original foundry in Fresnoy-le-Grand, France, and passes through the hands of at least 15 artisans. At The Cook's Station we carry Le Creuset Dutch ovens, braisers, stainless steel and nonstick cookware, kettles and replacement knobs. Shop by color or category below, or come see the colors side by side at our Buncombe Street shop in Greenville.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
